    "q-132606": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132606",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=2.$ Given that the point $P(2,\\frac{1}{2},1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=x+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+\\frac{1}{y}$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$",
      "worked_solution": "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(2,\\frac{1}{2}).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(2,\\frac{1}{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(2,\\frac{1}{2}) & =2+2(2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})+\\frac{1}{(1/2)} \\\\  & =2+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(2,\\frac{1}{2}) & ={f}_{y}(2,\\frac{1}{2})(y-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z-1 & =4(y-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z-1 & =4y-2 \\\\ z & =4y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(2,\\frac{1}{2},1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=4y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=2,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=4y-1$ (or $4y-z-1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,4,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,4,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =j+4\\,k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $⟨0,1,4⟩.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-132606-a",
